.TH garuda-toolbox-users-edit 1  "garuda-toolbox 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
garuda\-toolbox\-users\-edit \- Change an account\*(Aqs full name, login shell or groups
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgaruda\-toolbox users edit\fR [\fB\-\-full\-name\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-shell\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-add\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR] [\fB\-\-remove\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-move\-files\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR \fIWHEN\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR \fICOLUMNS\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIUSER\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change an account\*(Aqs full name, login shell or groups
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-full\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
The new full name. An empty one clears it
.TP
\fB\-\-shell\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
The new login shell, one of /etc/shells
.TP
\fB\-\-add\-group\fR \fI<GROUP>\fR
Join a group, as often as needed
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\-group\fR \fI<GROUP>\fR
Leave a group, as often as needed
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
A new home folder: its full path
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print the programs\*(Aq own words under an error
.TP
\fB\-\-move\-files\fR
Move the old home folder\*(Aqs files to the new one
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print long text directly instead of through `$PAGER`
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Colour the output: auto, always or never
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Do not ask, carry the change out. Needed without a terminal
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the plan and stop, without asking and without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<COLUMNS>\fR
Cut long cells to this many columns
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON Lines instead of text, for scripts. Needs `\-\-yes` or `\-\-dry\-run`
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Leave out the spinner and the hints
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIUSER\fR>
The account, as `users list` prints it
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  garuda\-toolbox users edit ada \-\-shell /usr/bin/fish
  garuda\-toolbox users edit ada \-\-add\-group docker \-\-remove\-group video
.SH "SEE ALSO"
garuda\-toolbox\-users(1), garuda\-toolbox(1)
